  <prompt>
    Deliver the committed stretch feature: Document Q&amp;A over the session-mounted document (FR-35). With the document in session context (a `Doc` ledger entry), the agent answers questions with citations per the ADR-039 grounded-output invariant — e.g. "what's the indemnification cap?" → cited answer + a navigated ephemeral highlight ("found in §7.3"). This rides the EXISTING Text-path / bounded agent loop and the R1 `compose-document` scope as session context — NO new capability, NO new playbook, NO new dispatch target. The real work is validation that the answer is grounded/cited and the ephemeral-highlight three-pane UX (Workspace highlight + Assistant citation + Context section/playbook surfacing).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    AI platform + React developer fluent in the ADR-039 grounded-output invariant, the Text-path bounded agent loop, session-context (Doc ledger) mounting, and the SpaarkeAi three-pane coordination.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A working Document Q&amp;A stretch flow: with the document session-mounted, a natural-language question returns a grounded, cited answer and navigates an ephemeral highlight to the source span, with the citation in the Assistant and the section/playbook surfaced in the Context pane. No new capability, playbook, or dispatch endpoint is introduced.
  </goal>

